      "text": "To evaluate $\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3}\\right\\rfloor$, we need to understand what the floor function $\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor$ represents. The floor function, denoted by $\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor$, is defined as the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$.\n\nLet's consider the value of $-\\frac{5}{3}$ directly. First, calculate the value of $-\\frac{5}{3}$, which is $-1.6667$ (or equivalently, $-1\\frac{2}{3}$).\n\nThe floor function $\\left\\lfloor -1.6667 \\right\\rfloor$ gives the greatest integer less than or equal to $-1.6667$. The integers immediately around $-1.6667$ are $-2$ and $-1$. Since $-1.6667$ is less than $-1$ (and greater than or equal to $-2$), the greatest integer less than or equal to $-1.6667$ is $-2$.\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\\[ \\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor -1.6667 \\right\\rfloor = -2 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-2}\n\\]",
